Developed a test scenario for Qualification Catalog specifically for a university context.

Purpose: To simulate a real-time example to present to the client during the upcoming session.

Created All Academic and Administrative Positions

Added key positions such as Vice Chancellor, Deans, Registrars, Directors, and HODs.

Aligned positions based on standard university organizational structure.

Built Qualification Catalog Structure

Created Qualification Groups (e.g., Faculty Skills, Management Skills, Research Skills).

Defined Qualifications under each group (e.g., Subject Expertise, Teaching Skills, Leadership).

Assigned Proficiency Levels (e.g., Beginner, Intermediate, Expert).

Mapped Qualifications to Positions

Mapped relevant qualifications to each position to demonstrate how qualification requirements align with role expectations.

Simulated Employee Qualification Data

Entered sample employee qualifications, experience, and proficiency for test employees.

Ensured data is available to showcase qualification matching and gap analysis.

Executed Succession Planning Analysis

Used the Qualification Catalog mapping to simulate potential successors for key roles.

Showcased how system identifies readiness and gaps based on actual qualifications.

