Daily BASIS support Activities.␀ABAP Work␀Cutover strategy discussion␀This week, I gained a comprehensive understanding of the Sales and Product Cost Model in Integrated Financial Planning (IFP) within SAP Analytics Cloud. I learned how sales quantity drives cost calculations by linking it to component structures and cost center resources using lot sizes. I explored how quantity structures define the standard component and resource usage per lot, and how these are scaled based on planned sales volume. Through data actions, I saw how COMPONENTQUANTITY and LOTSIZE are initialized from cost estimates, and how they are used to calculate required resource quantities and ultimately manufacturing overheads. I also understood the logic for calculating raw material inventory value and allocating costs to the correct GL accounts, enabling detailed and accurate product cost planning.␀1- Finance KPIs
