SCM session for KPIs Finalization␀currently working on two major Continuous Control Monitoring (CCM) tickets for our client, Packages, focusing on Purchase Order (PO) price variances:

Local POs Scenario: I successfully configured this rule using the GRC front-end. I mapped the standard tables (EKKO, EKPO, MBEW) and utilized the Net Price (EKPO-NETPR) to calculate variances against the material's Moving Average Price.

Import POs Scenario (Ticket #0478922): This requirement is more complex, as it requires pulling proposed pricing (PRCD_ELEMENTS) and actual delivery costs (EKBZ) to check for a &gt;10% variance. Because the GRC web UI restricts complex table chaining (Star-Join limitation), I have drafted a detailed Functional Specification Document (FSD) directing the ABAP team to build a custom Z Table and background job to support the logic.

Recent Learnings & Skill Development
Through these two tickets, I have significantly deepened my functional and technical SAP knowledge. Recently, I have been learning:

SAP Relational Table Architecture: I've mastered how purchasing and valuation tables connect, including critical nuances like joining Plant (WERKS) to Valuation Area (BWKEY) to prevent massive data duplication.

System Limitations & Workarounds: I now understand the hard limits of the GRC &quot;Table Setup&quot; tool and how to bypass them using SAP GUI backend tools like SQ02 (Infosets) and SE11 (Data Dictionary).

Technical Consulting: I am learning how to translate functional roadblocks into actionable technical requirements. I can now write formal FSDs that define exact inner-join logic and field mappings for ABAP developers.

SAP Data Structures: I've gained a better understanding of SAP field behavior&mdash;such as knowing that EBELN (PO Number) and KNUMV (Condition Number) cannot be joined, despite both being 10-character text strings, because they hold completely different data.␀BPD Draft and Sign Off␀Supporting daily operations at OGDCL by identifying and resolving users issues.␀Working on October payroll data correction .␀TRM customization meetings & ERP status meetings␀CGA Project␀Conducted FICO workshops with onsite team for Financial accounting, Controlling, Funds Management, PS & understanding of MM/SD␀A comprehensive overview session was conducted on the Assessment Cycle, integrating real business scenarios and aligned with both industry and SAP standard best practices. The discussion emphasized end to end processing using standard SAP functionality to ensure operational clarity and alignment with client requirements. All related activities were completed successfully, and additional details are available within the referenced ticket, which has been closed as per the client&rsquo;s expectations.␀currently working on two major Continuous Control Monitoring (CCM) tickets for our client, Packages, focusing on Purchase Order (PO) price variances:

