SAP Upgrade␀EBM onsite Visit and Planning sessions␀Gunvour Parco conversion and archiving␀EMCO Session with Customer Lahore␀CCL pharma Rise with SAP Meeting on request of Sofia␀For Datasphere, SAC and Rise connectivity all prerequisites documentation and initiation.␀TMC | Brookes Pharma | Technical & Functional Discussion␀Objective

To implement seamless integration between the EFFI platform and the KOHA Library Management System, enabling efficient data synchronization and improved user experience for students and administrators.

Key Features & Functional Requirements
Library Management System Integration
Establish seamless integration with the Koha Library Management System.
Ensure compatibility with existing library workflows and data structures.
User Data Synchronization
Enable automatic syncing of student credentials between EFFI and KOHA.
Maintain up-to-date borrowing privileges based on student status.
Reduce manual data entry and minimize synchronization errors.
Student Portal Access
Provide students with access to their library information through the EFFI portal, including:
Borrowing history
Issued and returned books
Pending and paid library fines
Automation & Real-Time Updates
Implement real-time or scheduled synchronization for:
User accounts
Book transactions
Fine records
Ensure data consistency across both systems.
Expected Outcomes
Improved efficiency in library operations
Enhanced user experience for students
Centralized access to academic and library services
Reduced administrative workload through automation␀8 April

