4) did modelling using the fact views␀Key Features & Functional Requirements
User Data Integration
Fetch user data (students, faculty, staff) from PeopleSoft into Koha.
Automatically create and update patron records in Koha.
Ensure accurate mapping of user fields (e.g., name, ID, department, contact details).
Automated Synchronization
Implement scheduled or real-time data synchronization between PeopleSoft and Koha.
Update user status (active/inactive) based on PeopleSoft records.
Eliminate manual entry of library users.
Patron Account Management
Assign appropriate borrower categories in Koha (student, faculty, staff).
Set borrowing privileges according to user roles defined in PeopleSoft.
Automatically deactivate users who are no longer active in PeopleSoft.
Data Consistency & Validation
Ensure data integrity during transfer between systems.
Handle duplicate records and prevent inconsistencies.
Validate mandatory fields before updating Koha.
Integration Mechanism
Use APIs, web services, or secure data exchange (e.g., JSON/XML).
Implement authentication and authorization for secure data transfer.
Log synchronization activities for monitoring and troubleshooting.
Expected Outcomes
Centralized and automated user management for the DUHS Library
Reduced administrative workload and manual errors
Real-time availability of accurate user data in Koha
Improved efficiency in library operations and user services␀Pending Form Report / Proceed Form Report␀1145-B1-2.7-HCM-02-SF-ECP-(2.7 Extensibility Design Review)
